{"id":"ea98968ac191af8c","group":"93","path":"93/93-thm-post-completeness.md","title":"Maximal-Consistent Theory Characterization","display":"Maximal-Consistent Theory Characterization","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-thm-post-completeness","aliases":["93-thm-post-completeness"],"display":"Maximal-Consistent Theory Characterization","depends_on":["[[93-df-classical-propositional-calculus]]","[[93-df-theory]]","[[93-df-consistency]]","[[93-df-maximal-theory]]","[[93-df-complete-theory]]","[[93-ax-boolean-completeness]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-thm-post-completeness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-thm-post-completeness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Maximal-Consistent Theory Characterization"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e3c8f5c9e577b791\" href=\"?note=e3c8f5c9e577b791\" title=\"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus\">93-df-classical-propositional-calculus</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"cf7108c33537548a\" href=\"?note=cf7108c33537548a\" title=\"93-df-theory\">93-df-theory</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"959f67178eec388a\" href=\"?note=959f67178eec388a\" title=\"93-df-consistency\">93-df-consistency</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"8bbd77b21a9519f1\" href=\"?note=8bbd77b21a9519f1\" title=\"93-df-maximal-theory\">93-df-maximal-theory</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"1bb65160feb13df8\" href=\"?note=1bb65160feb13df8\" title=\"93-df-complete-theory\">93-df-complete-theory</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"dc3498f98607795c\" href=\"?note=dc3498f98607795c\" title=\"93-ax-boolean-completeness\">93-ax-boolean-completeness</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"thm-post-completeness-—-Maximal-Consistent-Theory-Characterization\">thm-post-completeness — Maximal-Consistent Theory Characterization</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)\">\\(\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)\\)</span> is the concrete classical presentation of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"e3c8f5c9e577b791\" href=\"?note=e3c8f5c9e577b791\" title=\"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus\">93-df-classical-propositional-calculus</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}\\)</span> have their two-place signatures; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CompleteTh}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{CompleteTh}_{93}\\)</span> receives <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Neg}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\">\\(\\operatorname{Neg}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\)</span> explicitly.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}post\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)\n\\land\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(\\Gamma,\\mathsf L)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}(\\Gamma,\\mathsf L)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{CompleteTh}_{93}(\\Gamma;\\mathsf L,\n\\operatorname{Neg}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93})\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}post\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)\n\\land\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(\\Gamma,\\mathsf L)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}(\\Gamma,\\mathsf L)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{CompleteTh}_{93}(\\Gamma;\\mathsf L,\n\\operatorname{Neg}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93})\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>For a consistent theory of the formally presented classical calculus, maximal consistency is equivalent to deciding every formula. The presentation antecedent is essential.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"thm-post-completeness-—-Maximal-Consistent-Theory-Characterization","text":"thm-post-completeness — Maximal-Consistent Theory Characterization","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus","status":"resolved","id":"e3c8f5c9e577b791","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-classical-propositional-calculus]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-theory","status":"resolved","id":"cf7108c33537548a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-theory]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-consistency","status":"resolved","id":"959f67178eec388a","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-consistency]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-maximal-theory","status":"resolved","id":"8bbd77b21a9519f1","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-maximal-theory]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-complete-theory","status":"resolved","id":"1bb65160feb13df8","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-complete-theory]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-ax-boolean-completeness","status":"resolved","id":"dc3498f98607795c","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-ax-boolean-completeness]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus","status":"resolved","id":"e3c8f5c9e577b791","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)$ is the concrete classical presentation of [[93-df-classical-propositional-calculus]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CompleteTh}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Neg}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}post\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)\n\\land\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(\\Gamma,\\mathsf L)\\\\\n&\\to\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}(\\Gamma,\\mathsf L)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{CompleteTh}_{93}(\\Gamma;\\mathsf L,\n\\operatorname{Neg}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93})\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":1349,"backlinks":[],"outgoing":["e3c8f5c9e577b791","cf7108c33537548a","959f67178eec388a","8bbd77b21a9519f1","1bb65160feb13df8","dc3498f98607795c"]}